# Bank 11 (runs at 0x8000). Directives: L label, C line comment, B block
# header, D data range, F row width.
#
# THIS BANK HOLDS NO CODE. It is the first half of the MAP: it is always
# mapped together with bank 12 (0xA000) (p00:4552-p00:455C,
# p00:460E-p00:4618, p00:5CE1-p00:5CEB and p00:5D84-p00:5D8E), so for the
# scroll code they are 16 KB in a row from 0x8000 to 0xBFFF.
#
# HOW THE BACKGROUND IS DRAWN. Routine 0x46DF in bank 0 takes a byte from the
# stage's script, multiplies it by 16 and adds it to 0x8000 (or to 0x8FF0 in
# stages 5, 9, 10 and 12, p00:46F2-p00:4708). What is there is sixteen bytes:
# a column of four characters taken four at a time. In other words, each byte
# of the script is a PIECE of 4x4 characters, and the whole map is written
# with those pieces.

B 0x8000 BACKGROUND PIECES AND STAGE SCRIPTS (bank 11)

D 0x8000 0x8FF0 pieces_A  255 pieces of 16 bytes each (4x4 characters). The index comes from the stage's script; 0x470B adds 16*index to 0x8000.
F 0x8000 16
D 0x8FF0 0x97DE pieces_B  The other set of pieces, based at 0x8FF0. Used by stages 5, 9, 10 and 12 (0x46F5-0x4706 compares 0xE061 with 5, 9, 10 and 12).
F 0x8FF0 16
D 0x97DE 0x97F8 script_table  Thirteen words, one per stage: where that stage's script starts. Read by 0x46C3 with 0x47AE. Entry 0 is 0x0000 (there is no stage 0); 1 to 6 point into this bank and 7 onwards into bank 12.
F 0x97DE w2
D 0x97F8 0xA000 scripts_1  The scripts of stages 1 to 6 (0x97F8, 0x99A8, 0x9B58, 0x9D08 and 0x9F18), one after another. Rows of six bytes.
F 0x97F8 6
